### Cron Expression Examples

The user's local timezone is **${n}**. Cron expressions and \`run_once_at\` timestamps are always in UTC. When the user says a local time, convert it to UTC but confirm with them: "9am ${n} = Xam UTC, so the cron would be \`0 X * * 1-5\`." For one-time runs, the same conversion applies \u2014 "run this at 3pm" \u2192 \`"run_once_at": "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:00:00Z"\` with their 3pm converted to UTC.

